 @JazerMedia  There are levels of ray tracing. No GPU now or in the foreseeable future will ever provide full, real-time PBR ray tracing.
RTX provides basic light paths, and superficial materials and lighting. Given the dynamic environments, this is more than good enough for all but the most demanding of gamers.
When you talk about needing orders of magnitude faster, you are not truly comparing like with like. A single 4K ray traced scene in Blender or 3DS can take minutes or hours to render. No GPU is attempting that level of realism, but I suspect that the average gamer is not even sensitive to caustics, SSS shading, high bounce and refraction levels, PBR shaders, GI lighting, or any of the other things that divide them.

